  <event id="205">
      <start>10:00</start>
      <duration>01:00</duration>
      <room>AW1.126</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>Monitoring MySQL</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>MySQL</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Over the past 18 months different open source monitoring solutions have popped up, some of them with a lot of potential. Zabbix, Zenoss and Hyperic are probably the most famous ones but other more specialized ones exist.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Last year we evaluated these Monitoring solutions and presented our findings at OLS. As we are MySQL users we obviously wanted to take a closer look at these tools regarding their integration with MySQL.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This talk therefore will guide the MySQL users around in a selection of Open Source Monitoring tools that they could use to monitor MySQL as a part of a bigger infrastructure.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="2051">Kris Buytaert</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>